<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The resurrect mech ability's warmup effect, played on the clicked corpse for the length of
    the cast (AbilityDefs/ResurrectMech.xml names it through VEF's
    AbilityExtension_WarmupEffecter, which spawns it at the corpse and ticks it against the
    corpse until the warmup ends). Biotech's ApocrionAoeWarmup (sic, 1.7.4990, Biotech
    Defs/Effects/Effecter_Misc.xml) sized for one mech: the apocriton's marks the 5 cell area
    its cast picks corpses up from, a pulsing wave 10 cells across and sparks anywhere within
    4.5 cells of the centre, and this ability brings back the one clicked mech.

    Both children are the apocriton's but for their size. Vanilla's mech bodies draw between
    1.1 cells (a lifter) and 3 (a centipede, a war queen, a diabolus), so the effect is sized
    for the largest and stays close around the smallest:
    - The sparks land within positionRadius 1.5 of the corpse, the half width of a 3 cell
      body, against 4.5. chancePerTick 0.03 against 0.05: the area is a ninth of the
      apocriton's, so its rate would crowd it; 0.03 is seven sparks over the default 4 second
      warmup.
    - The wave is the apocriton's Mote_ApocritonWarmupArea at scale 0.4, 4 cells across
      against 10 (SubEffecter_Sprayer multiplies the mote's drawSize by the child's scale), a
      ring around a heavy mech and a cell clear of a light one. Its texture fades toward the
      rim, so it reads narrower than it draws.
  -->
  <EffecterDef>
    <defName>OLWC_ResurrectWarmup</defName>
    <children>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerChance</subEffecterClass>
        <moteDef>Mote_MechSparkSimple</moteDef>
        <burstCount>1</burstCount>
        <chancePerTick>0.03</chancePerTick>
        <rotation>-150~-150</rotation>
        <spawnLocType>OnTarget</spawnLocType>
        <scale>1.0~1.3</scale>
        <positionRadius>1.5</positionRadius>
      </li>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerTriggered</subEffecterClass>
        <moteDef>Mote_ApocritonWarmupArea</moteDef>
        <burstCount>1</burstCount>
        <rotation>-150~150</rotation>
        <scale>0.4</scale>
        <positionRadius>0</positionRadius>
        <spawnLocType>OnTarget</spawnLocType>
      </li>
    </children>
  </EffecterDef>
</Defs>
